problems.problem:
In order to use an Automated Teller Machine (ATM) of a bank, a customer must type his personal identification number PIN (an integer). The customer may give the code 3 times only. If the correct code is given then the message «Επιτυχής Πρόσβαση» ("Successful Access") is displayed. Otherwise, each time the code is wrong, the message «Λάθος κωδικός» ("Wrong code") is displayed and the code is requested again with the message «Προσπαθήστε ξανά» ("Try again") until the 3rd attempt has also been made.

The program below was created for the above operation. The program contains at least 4 errors (logical and/or syntax). Write in your answer book 4 of them, stating **ONLY** the number of the line in which each error appears **together with the corrected statement**.

```Pascal
{1} Program askisi8;
{2} uses wincrt;
{3} const
{4}     code = 1234;
{5} var
{6} try, pin:integer;
{7} access:string;

{8} begin
{9}     try:=0;

{10}   repeat
{11}          write('Δώσε PIN: ');
{12}          readln(pin);
{13}
{14}          If pin = code then
{15}             access:= true
{16}          else
{17}              begin
{18}                  access:=false;
{19}                  try:=try - 1;
{20}                  writeln('Λάθος κωδικός ');
{21}                  if 3-try <> 0 then
{22}                  writeln('Προσπαθήστε ξανά');
{23}              end
{24}     until (access = true) OR  (try > 3);
{25}     If access then
{26}        writeln('Επιτυχής Πρόσβαση ');
{27}     else
{28}        writeln('Αποτυχία πρόσβασης')
{29} end.
```

