problems.problem:
A ball is dropped from a height of Y centimetres and begins to bounce. Because of the energy lost on impact with the ground after each bounce, the ball reaches a height equal to 80% of the height it had reached in the previous bounce. The program below accepts as input the initial height Y and for each bounce calculates and displays the number and the height of each bounce. Assume that the bounces stop when the bounce height becomes less than or equal to one centimetre (1 cm).

The program contains logical and/or syntax errors. Write in your answer book four of them, stating **the line number** in which each error appears **together with the corrected statement**. (Assume that the statement in line {2} is correct.)

```Pascal
 {1}  program askisi6;
 {2}  uses wincrt;
 {3}  const one := 1;
 {4}  var  c : integer;
 {5}         Y : real;
 {6}  begin
 {7}      c := 80;
 {8}      writeln('Δώσε ύψος: ');
 {9}      writeln(Y);
{10}      while Y < 1 do
{11}         begin
{12}            c := c + one;
{13}            Y := Y - Y *0.80;
{14}            writeln(‘αριθμός αναπήδησης: ‘,c, ‘ ύψος αναπήδησης: ‘, Y:4:2)
{15}         end
{16}  end.
```

