problems.problem:
The program below, written in the Pascal programming language, is given. Using the dry-run method, present the results of the program when the values 7 -3 8 -2 are given to the variable **timi**. In place of a space use the symbol «□».

```Pascal
program askisi7;
uses wincrt;
var k, n, total, timi : integer;
     neg: boolean;
begin
        total:=0;
        k:=0;
        n:=9;
        neg:=false;
        repeat
                readln (timi);
                If timi >0 then
                         total:=total+timi
                else
                         neg:=true;
                k:=k+3;
        until (k>n) and (neg=true);
        writeln('Τέλος προγράμματος',total:3,timi:3)
end.
```

