problems.problem:
The program below has been written for a shop in order to calculate and print the number of products that a customer buys and the final price he will pay for all the products. The shop employee enters the price of each product into the system. The repetition stops when he gives a product price of zero. On the price of each product 18% VAT is calculated and added. At the end, if the total price including VAT that the customer will pay exceeds 100 euros then a discount of 10% on the total price is given, otherwise a discount of 5% is given. The final price is calculated by subtracting the discount from the total price.

The program contains logical and/or syntax errors. Write in your answer book four (4) of them, stating **the line number** in which each error appears **together with the corrected statement**. (Assume that the statement in line {2} is correct.)

```Pascal
