problems.problem:
A shop owner decided to offer to a charitable foundation, as a donation, the decimal part (cents) of every receipt that exceeds 50 euros.

The following program in the Pascal programming language was created to accept from the user the amount of a receipt and then to calculate and print the possible amount the foundation will receive from that receipt. If the amount of the receipt does not exceed 50 euros or the decimal part is zero cents, it prints the message «Καμία δωρεά από αυτή την είσπραξη!» (No donation from this receipt!). The repetition stops when a receipt of zero or a negative number is given. At the end, the total donation in euros that the foundation will receive is printed.

*Examples:*

If the receipt is 56.75 euros, then the 0.75 euros will be given to the foundation.

If the receipt is 40.50 (that is, less than 50.00 euros) or 60.00 euros (that is, the decimal part (cents) is 0), then the foundation will not receive any amount.

The program contains logical and/or syntax errors. Write in your answer booklet six (6) of them, stating **the number of the line** in which each error appears **together with the corrected statement** (assume that the statement in line {2} is correct).

```Pascal
