The following program in the C++ programming language is given:

```C++
#include <iostream>
#include <iomanip>
#include <cmath>
using namespace std;
int main(){
int n1,n2,n3,n4;
float r1,r2;
cin >> n1 >> n2 >> n3;
 [ Α ]
if( [ Β ] ){
   [ Γ ]
   [ Δ ]
}
 [ Ε ]
return 0;
}
```

Write in your answer book:

(a) The statement that must be placed at **position Α** so that the average of the values of the variables n1, n2 and n3 is assigned to the variable **r1**.

(b) The condition that must be placed at **position Β**, which checks whether the variable **n1** is not equal to the variable **n2** or whether the variable **n1** is equal to the variable **n3**.

(c) The statement that must be placed at **position Γ** so that the sum of the units digits of the variables n1 and n2 is assigned to the variable **n4**.

(d) The statement that must be placed at **position Δ** so that the integer part of the variable **r1** is assigned to the variable **r2**.

(e) The statement that must be placed at **position Ε** so that the value of the variable **r1** is printed with a precision of two (2) decimal digits.

